  "task": {
    "objective": "Each merchant needs two units of its required kind at its own depot. Initially nobody owns the kind they need. Negotiate through visible recipient quotes, physical deposits, conditional cycles or unsecured gifts, then transport the newly owned goods.",
    "natural_termination": "Every merchant has delivered two required-kind goods. Otherwise truncate at 120 steps. A natural completion on step 120 takes priority. Terminal raw state is absorbing.",
    "interaction": "Ownership, carrier, commitment, recipient and lock timer belong to each physical good. Whole compatible bilateral or three-party cycles transfer title only after all offers mature. Goods stay on the seller's actual pad after settlement and must be fetched. Withdrawing before settlement prevents the whole dependent cycle; gifts bypass that protection and can be claimed or withheld. Merchants compete for occupied corridor cells and finite time.",
    "observation_access": "All cargo positions, ownership, carriers, escrow commitments, timers, quotes, depot needs and event flags are public. Every entity visibility mask is true. The static walls and pad/depot geometry are public. No text messages or extra renderer-only policy information exist."
  },
